WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.180
Ethan: Aw man!

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.040
I'm so upset!

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.420
I just realized...

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.680
I went to this place last night,
and this is not relevant at all,

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.120
but I got pickled carrots
and pickled beans,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.980
and I left them at Mika's house.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.200
(Ethan sighs)

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.640
Mark: That's really sad. (Sarcastically)
Tyler: Aw man. (Sarcastically)

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.420
Mark: Welcome back to Markiplier Makes.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.540
This time, we're making pies.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:24.380
And pies, as we all know are...

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.600
part of... American culture specifically,

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.980
and they would put mutton in there,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.100
they would put some intestines...

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.920
Can uh... whoever is editing this,

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:39.900
maybe it's me.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.580
Editor Mark: It's me.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.980
Mark: Can you put a- can you put a- uh..

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.060
Can you put a mouse in this, and just put
a lot of blood, and real gory sound effects?

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.260
Editor Mark: No.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.960
Mark: Put a mouse in this.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.780
(Mark laughs maniacally)
(classic horror movie music plays)

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:56.280
Mark: Alright, I just wanted to...

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.960
(all laugh)

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.400
Mark: That would be a really good joke.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.920
Evolution of pie: came from meat,
went to VEGETABLES first -

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.440
Not many people know this - Vegetables
got their way into their pastries.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.840
You got the carrot cakes,
you got your potato cakes...

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.480
Ethan: What is your
opinion on carrot cake?

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.000
Mark: I love it!

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.360
Ethan: I think it's good, and
everyone gives me shit for it!

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.780
Tyler: I like carrot cake.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.340
Mark: Why would everybody? What's wrong
with-- carrot cake is delicious!

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.220
Ethan: I don't know!! It's so good!
Tyler: Listen, carrot cake is delicious.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.460
Ethan: And nobody likes it!

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.040
Mark: It's got a really rich,
not too sweet taste to it.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.080
Tyler: Especially the cinnamon
and the nutmeg to it.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.880
Mark: Oh yeah..
Ethan: It's really good-

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.500
'cause I think that most cake is like
a little- a little overwhelming-

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.900
Mark: Oh, most people who have cake.
It's still like, way too sweet.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.300
Ethan: Yeah.
Mark: Yeah.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.720
Tyler: They put too much icing on it.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:37.640
Ethan: Carrot cake is so good.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.240
Mark: Like we did when we made cake.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:39.960
Ethan: Yeah.
Tyler: Yeah.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.340
Ethan: Did we make cake?

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.140
Tyler: Yeah.
Mark: Yeah, we did.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:45.480
Mark: Let's cut to the moment where we said,
"cake needs to be sweeter than hell."

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.900
And like, "everything needs
to be overly sugary."

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.900
(Mark grunts and moans)

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:51.000
Mark: Gotta put a little more sugar!

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.000
Mark: Oh shit, that was too much sugar.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.420
(Mark &amp; Tyler laugh)

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.420
(classy music plays)

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.640
Mark: And now...
(classy music plays)

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.860
Tyler says some Random Bullshit.
(classy music plays)

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.860
Tyler: Hey listen, I had
a great dream last night,

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:04.380
Mark: Uh-huh.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.020
Tyler: It was about Mickey Mouse,

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.780
and he was chopping up carrots
that were screaming.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.400
Mark: Alright.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.300
So pie...

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.300
So we're gonna make some pie,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.060
we're gonna eat some pie,

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.300
and we're gonna do this
all with knowing...

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.880
that... (sniffs)

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.880
pies are made with love

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.400
and you need to have love to make pie.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.480
Make pie, not love.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.900
Ethan: Uh okay... I don't know.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.000
(all laugh)

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.180
Ethan: "Sex is great, but you ever have a pie?"

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.620
(all laugh)

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.340
Mark: We have... we have pie crust mix.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.220
We're not gonna use it.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.200
(Spongebob "My leg!" sound effect)

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.300
(Ethan groans in dismay)

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.680
Mark: We don't need it. None of that.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.780
Mark: Not important... That's fine.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.680
Mark: It's really simple
ingredients to make pie crust.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.500
Mark: The important thing that I learned
from all my cooking shows that I've seen,

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.720
Mark: I'm gonna keep to myself
and not tell you guys.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.020
You're on your own.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.480
Fuck you Assholes.
I'm going for it. (chuckles)

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.720
Ethan: I'm going to wash my hands,

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.340
as all good chefs should!

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:10.780
Ethan: (in the distance) I have.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.380
Tyler: I already washed mine.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.040
Mark: Wait, just rub your
washed hands on my hands.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.100
Mark: They'll be clean!
(Tyler giggles)

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.480
Mark: Perfect, that's perfect.
Alright, that's great.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:20.080
Mark: (blows into his bowl loudly)

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:20.940
Tyler: Wait...

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.900
Ethan: Did you spit in mine?

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.460
No, not mine.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.880
Mark: You always assume I'm doing something bad

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.180
again- against for you.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.180
That's not true. (giggles)

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.640
(boom)

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.920
Ethan: I didn't, oh I don't
know why... I don't know why.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:37.780
Tyler: Oh look at that...

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:38.280
Ethan: OHhohoh!

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.800
Ethan: Anyone see this?

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.060
Wow.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.220
Mark: It doesn't help that
I'm trying to measure the water

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.460
when I haven't measured
anything else ever in this.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.960
Mark: It's reaching
about this consistency

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.460
which I don't think is correct.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.220
Ethan: A measuring cup!

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.600
Where are the whisks?

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.520
Mark: I don't know. Maybe
there aren't whisks, I don't know.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.760
Ethan: There are no whisks?

00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.780
Mark: I don't know.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.980
Ethan: What kind of kitchen are we running?!

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:02.820
Hey!

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.720
I used too much egg...

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.720
(Mark &amp; Ethan laugh)

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:08.880
Mark: Did you now?

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.880
Ethan: It's just straight yellow, dude.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.300
Maybe if I just add more of other things...

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.860
Mark: Hmm.
Ethan: .. it'll make it better.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.400
Ethan: Ugh, how much time do we have?

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.640
Mark: Uh...

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.540
Mark: We have, put-- get the timer up.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.380
Mark: We have... five minutes!

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.240
Starting now, go!

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.980
Ethan: Mine isn't good...
I broke the whisk I think.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.240
Mark: Why did you do that?

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:32.920
Ethan: I didn't mean to.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.300
Mark: What are you talking about?

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.700
Mark: You need to develop the glutens.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.900
(Mark slams dough loudly)

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.300
Ethan: I don't think this is good.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.220
(Ethan laughs)

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:44.500
Mark: It's really yellow.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.160
Tyler: So is mine.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:46.940
Mark: Wow.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.080
Ethan: I put turmeric in it.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.600
Tyler: How many eggs did you use?

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.600
Ethan: Three!
Tyler: I put two!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.600
Mark: I put one. Oh, darn it.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:57.220
(all laugh)

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.260
Mark: Wow, that looks like squash.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.800
It looks like baby food.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.080
Ethan: This is God awful!

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.520
This is really, really bad.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.060
Tyler: Ethan, I think we're both
pretty bad boys with the egg.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.540
Ethan: Oh no! How did it get over there?

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.260
Mark: Oh my God... Oh my God!

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.040
Ethan: AHHGGGHHHH

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.200
Can I start over?

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:18.820
Mark: No! How much time do we got?

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.180
Tyler: Can I have some more flour, Ethan?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.640
Ethan: I have a feeling my pie
is gonna be best pie.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:25.200
Tyler: You've got this Ethan,
I believe in you.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.340
Mark: My pie, best pie.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:30.100
Ethan: Now THAT is a pie crust.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:35.120
(Mark &amp; Tyler laugh)

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:38.880
Ethan: I've never seen
anything quite like this.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:42.640
Marl: Y'know, me neither.
I have not. You are right.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.900
Ethan: I don't know where to go.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.060
Mark: Add more flour, you idiot!

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.720
Ethan: Give me the flour.
(Mark laughs)

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.360
Mark: I'm gonna get so many
bits of paper in mine.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.220
(Tyler &amp; Amy giggle)

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.220
Tyler: My God!

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.180
Ethan: Don't look over here!

00:05:59.180 --> 00:05:59.680
Mark: Okay.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.100
Get this out of my way!

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.800
(Ethan laughs)
(Tyler coughs)

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.620
Ethan: What are you doing?

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:10.380
(Mark beats dough violently
with a rolling pin)

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:16.580
(Mark continues to abuse dough)

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.780
Mark: I've seen this on the,
uh, Discovery Channel...

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:19.640
Er, uh, duh...

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.600
Bir- Brish Bakin'
(Great British Baking Off)

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.600
Mark: You gotta fold LAYERS of butter.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.800
Ethan: I've never seen
anything like this before.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.520
Tyler: I've never seen that ever.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.340
Mark: You gotta fold layers
of butter! That's what it is!

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:31.680
Mark: That's what pastry is!

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.000
Mark: Oh... yes.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:35.880
(Tyler laughs)

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.100
Mark: (triumphantly) Yes I am!

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.620
Mark: Oh God.
Ethan: I'm feeling good.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.580
I'm gonna have a hundred layers...

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.580
if I do a layer a second.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:48.140
Ethan: This is mint dough.
This dough is really up there.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.340
Mark: "This is mint dough."

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.200
Oh God, there's butter
leaking everywhere.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:53.940
Oh God.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.360
It's so buttery and delicious.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:00.200
Oh God, oh God, oh God!

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.080
Amy: Time's up!

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.340
Mark: What?! No countdown?!

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:04.380
Mark &amp; Tyler: Alright.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.260
Mark: Pie crust...?

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.700
Mark: Did you just taste that?
Ethan: Yeah.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:10.500
(Tyler laughs)

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:15.260
Mark: Alright, mine's got a little
butter leakage, but I think that's okay.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.020
Ethan: Mine looks good.
Mark: Now we need to let these chill.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:17.760
Ethan: Chill.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:18.780
(timer goes off)

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.560
