It was not time's up...

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:21.680
(The X-Files theme plays)

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.480
Amy: It said zero!

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.900
Amy: I don't know what's happening.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.340
Amy: I swear it said zero.
Tyler: We've been cheated of precious seconds.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:30.580
Ethan: Have a taste.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.060
Mark: I'm okay, thank you.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.940
Mark: I don't want a GIF of this to exist.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:35.760
Ethan: Well it's about to...

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.980
Mark: Why'd you stick
your finger in my mouth?

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.980
Ethan: For entertainment.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.340
It's good, right?

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.340
How about your dough?
Does it taste any better?

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:47.820
Mark: If I-- Well I'm not
gonna taste my dough.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:48.720
E c H!

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:49.840
Alright so we need to let 'em--

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.080
Eugh.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:53.280
We need to let 'em chill.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.620
We will now chill, for one hour,
to let it chill,

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.620
and then we will be back with the

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.620
(weird accent) FILLINGSSS!

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.520
Mark: Round TWooOOOoo!

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.300
Alright, the filling is the
most important part of any pie.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.240
Tell them about it.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:09.340
Ethan: OH~ If you don't have
a filling in your pie,

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.300
you don't have a pie,

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.440
ffffuck-hole!
(all laugh)

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.620
Mark: Alright so we need
to make the filling,

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.440
but we only have so much filling.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.600
We've got a lotta apples.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.860
Who wants to make apple pie?

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:24.180
I'll do the apples. (while laughing)
I've definitely got enough dough...

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.480
to do apples.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:26.620
Mark: Alright man.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:28.060
Ethan: I'll go whole hog.

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.640
Mark: Imma do apple,
raspberry, blueberry pie.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.140
Ethan: Alright.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:33.500
Amy: A pie does call for
three pounds of apples.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.000
Tyler: Like I said.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.600
Mark: No, no, no, no, this is like,
what, this is like ten pounds?

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.560
Okay they're three pounds.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.540
Mark: No! We're not gonna fight over it.
Ethan: Apple!

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.260
Ethan: Yes!

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.760
This shit's nuts!

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:46.860
Mark: You didn't core it.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.560
Ethan: I don't know how.
Tyler: You didn't put the hole--
Mark: The core--

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.000
Ethan: Core me.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:53.460
Mark: Core me daddy~!

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:54.260
Ethan: Ha ha!

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.200
This is so cool.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.100
Mark: Yeah!

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.980
Make it- uh, eight minutes.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:02.540
We've got eight minutes to make it.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.540
Can you hurry the hell up?

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.100
Ethan: I'm going as fast as I can.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:07.900
Mark: I'm gonna hand peel these

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.500
and we're gonna see which one of us
can make it faster, okay?

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.220
Ethan: Okay, but you also have to core your apples.
Mark: Yeah, I know.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:16.120
Ethan: I don't think that you think
it's as easy as you think it might be.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.120
Mark: Dude, I grew up poor.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.460
Mark: We used to core apples
day in, day out. (Ethan scoffs)

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:22.180
Mark: You don't tell me
about my heritage!

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.100
Tyler: That's how Mark fed his family.
Mark: Yeah!

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.460
Mark: That's how we made money,
selling them. The cores.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.000
Tyler: They just ate the cores that he cored.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.800
Mark: Well, no. That's how my family died
from all the cyanide.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:32.980
Tyler: What?
Ethan: The only cores

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.400
Ethan: that I do is the nice refreshing taste of...
Mark: Cyanide is naturally--

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.720
Mark: Shut up! Shut up!
Science! Science facts!

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.640
Z O O M !

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:42.420
In apple seeds, there's
